{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["But the land shall be forsaken — in the reckoning of the annulment of the oaths it will be satisfied and their iniquity will be atoned. And then — ״And I will remember״ etc." "וְתֵרַץ — from רצה, like וַיִּבֶן from בנה. יַעַן וּבְיַעַן, וּבְמִשְׁפָּטַי מָאֲסוּ וְאֶת חֻקּוֹתַי גְּעֲלָה נַפְשָׁם — יַעַן: וּבְמִשְׁפָּטַי מָאֲסוּ. וּבְיַעַן: וְאֶת חֻקּוֹתַי גְּעֲלָה נַפְשָׁם."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The comment reads ויתרצה as a passive form ('will be satisfied') and interprets the land's desolation as compensating for Israel's failure to let it rest in the sabbatical years; יכופר is impersonal passive.", 1 "Rashbam parses ותרץ as from רצה 'to be pleased/satisfied', citing the analogy of ויִבן from בנה to show a weak-letter root producing this form; he then maps the paired conjunctions יען and ביען onto the two parallel clauses that follow."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:49:36.980623640Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}